diagnosis_text:
The affected component is pc_0_0’s L3 host configuration (default gateway). Off-subnet traffic from pc_0_0 is being forwarded to a non-existent next-hop, which explains why only local-subnet pings (e.g., 10.0.0.1) work while everything across the fabric fails. Localization: on pc_0_0, eth0 is configured 10.0.0.2/24, and the routing table shows “default via 10.0.0.254 dev eth0.” An ip route lookup for 10.0.1.2 confirms it selects 10.0.0.254 as the next-hop. Probing shows ping 10.0.0.1 succeeds, but ping 10.0.0.254 fails with “Destination Host Unreachable” sourced from 10.0.0.2, and the ARP table shows “10.0.0.254 dev eth0 FAILED.” This indicates the kernel cannot resolve the configured gateway’s MAC because that IP is not present on the segment. Mechanism: with an invalid default gateway, pc_0_0 never forwards off-subnet traffic to the leaf; the kernel returns immediate host-unreachable errors locally, creating the appearance that the entire fabric is down from this host. Root cause: pc_0_0’s default route was misconfigured to 10.0.0.254 during the maintenance task; the correct gateway is the leaf at 10.0.0.1. Corrective fix: on pc_0_0, remove the bad route (ip route del default via 10.0.0.254) and add the correct one (ip route add default via 10.0.0.1 dev eth0), then make the change persistent in the host’s network config. After this, off-subnet connectivity should be restored. 
=== END ===